.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt IPCS 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ipcs
.Nd report System V interprocess communication facilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl abcMmopQqSsTt
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reports the System V message queues, shared memory segments and semaphore
sets in the system.
With no options it reports all three kinds, one line per object with its
kind, identifier, key, mode, owner and group.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Show everything:
.Fl b , c , o , p
and
.Fl t .
.It Fl b
Show the maximum sizes: the bytes a message queue may hold, a segment's
size, the number of semaphores in a set.
.It Fl c
Show the user and group of the object's creator.
.It Fl M
Show the shared memory limits.
.It Fl m
Report shared memory segments.
.It Fl o
Show outstanding usage: the bytes and messages on a queue, the number of
processes attached to a segment.
.It Fl p
Show process IDs: the last to send and to receive on a queue, a segment's
creator and the last to attach or detach it.
.It Fl Q
Show the message queue limits.
.It Fl q
Report message queues.
.It Fl S
Show the semaphore limits.
.It Fl s
Report semaphore sets.
.It Fl T
Show all the limits.
.It Fl t
Show times: of the last send, receive and change of a queue; the last
attach, detach and change of a segment; the last operation on and change of
a semaphore set.
.It Fl u Ar user
Report only the objects
.Ar user ,
a name or a number, owns.
.El
.Pp
The mode column has two letters of state before the permissions: a
.Ql D
for a segment removed while still attached, which goes once the last
process detaches; an
.Ql R
or
.Ql S
for a queue a process is waiting to receive from or to send to.
The permissions read like those of
.Xr ls 1 ,
with
.Ql a
for alter.
.Pp
.Nm
reads the kernel's tables,
.Va kern.ipc.msqids ,
.Va kern.ipc.shmsegs
and
.Va kern.ipc.sema .
When
.Va security.bsd.see_other_uids
is 0, a user other than the superuser sees only objects whose owner or
creator is that user's real user ID.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipcrm 1 ,
.Xr msgget 2 ,
.Xr semget 2 ,
.Xr shmget 2 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
is in the X/Open System Interfaces option of
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Fl M , Q , S , T
and
.Fl u
are extensions, from
.Fx .
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in AT&T System V.
OxideBSD's first appeared in 0.3.0, replacing BusyBox's.
